#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Generate the LaTeX bodies of every auto-generated paper table.

Reads the canonical result files under ``data/`` and emits one ``\\\\``-
terminated row block per paper table to a single file (default
``paper_tables.tex`` at the repo root). Each block is preceded by a
``% === <label> ===`` separator so it can be located by grep or copied
into the corresponding ``tabular*`` block of the paper.

Tables emitted (paper labels):
  tab:main-hard               natural-vs-hard accuracy across 4 encoders
  tab:cross-model             base vs DPT, 11-ds natural mean + 875 hard
  tab:main                    abridged 7-model main results
  tab:full-main               full 25-model main results (= App A)
  tab:probes                  ideal-point scorer + 3 structural relaxations
  tab:scorer-extensions       ideal-point + 3 capacity-adders
  tab:rank-ablation           LoRA rank ablation
  tab:rank-saturation         per-topic scorer rank sweep
  tab:paired-test             participant-level Wilcoxon + McNemar
  tab:cluster-coherence       Remesh cluster within-across lift
  tab:likert-correlation      pooled Spearman with Likert ratings
  tab:probe-on-tuned          per-topic probe on base vs DPT-tuned encoder
  tab:probe-on-tuned-margin   margin decomposition (needs probe_margin
                              _decomposition.json — run the corresponding
                              experiment first)

Tables not emitted by this script:
  tab:example                 illustrative anchor/match/distractor row, manual
  tab:errors                  LLM-classified error categories. The classifier
                              lives at scripts/experiments/classify_errors.py
                              and writes data/results/error_classification
                              .json; the 6-category counts are stable and
                              kept hand-typed in the paper rather than auto-
                              emitted here.
  table:datasets              auto-generated by scripts/plotting/
                              table_dataset_stats.py (writes dataset_stats
                              .tex at the repo root).

Usage:
  python scripts/build_paper_tables.py                 # writes paper_tables.tex
  python scripts/build_paper_tables.py --stdout        # prints to stdout
  python scripts/build_paper_tables.py --only tab:main # filter to one label
"""
